    <string name="guide_title">How to use GSD</string>
    <string name="guide_board">One board, one capture bar</string>
    <string name="guide_board_matrix_title">The matrix</string>
    <string name="guide_board_matrix_body">Your home view sorts tasks into four quadrants. A phone stacks them, and a tablet shows the full 2×2 board.</string>
    <string name="guide_board_capture_title">The capture bar</string>
    <string name="guide_board_capture_body">Every task starts in the bar at the top. Type the task, and GSD sends it to a quadrant from the ! and * markers you include.</string>
    <string name="guide_quadrants">The four quadrants</string>
    <string name="guide_q1">Urgent and important: crises and deadlines. Handle now.</string>
    <string name="guide_q2">Important, not urgent: strategy and growth. Protect time.</string>
    <string name="guide_q3">Urgent, not important: interruptions. Hand these off.</string>
    <string name="guide_q4">Neither: noise. Stop doing these.</string>
    <string name="guide_syntax">Quick-add syntax</string>
    <string name="guide_syntax_body">GSD reads the markers as you type, and the chip at the end of the capture bar shows where the task will land.</string>
    <string name="guide_syntax_urgent">Marks the task urgent</string>
    <string name="guide_syntax_both">Urgent and important (Do First)</string>
    <string name="guide_syntax_important">Marks the task important</string>
    <string name="guide_syntax_tag">Adds a tag</string>
    <string name="guide_syntax_link">Moves the link to the task\'s notes</string>
    <string name="guide_syntax_example_result">Creates an urgent, important task tagged #work and #q2.</string>
    <string name="guide_due">Due dates and reminders</string>
    <string name="guide_due_dates_title">Due dates</string>
    <string name="guide_due_dates_body">In the editor, choose Today, This week (Friday), Next week (Monday), or Pick a date. A task is all day until you tap All day under its date and set a time.</string>
    <string name="guide_reminders_title">Reminders</string>
    <string name="guide_reminders_body">A task with a due time reminds you before that time: 15 minutes by default, or what you pick in the editor or in Settings › Notifications. An all-day task reminds you at 9 AM on its due day, or that many days earlier when its reminder is a day or more before. Quiet hours hold a reminder until they end. The notification has Complete and Snooze 1 hour buttons.</string>
    <string name="guide_escalation_title">Escalating</string>
    <string name="guide_escalation_body">When a task that isn\'t marked urgent is due within two days, or is overdue, its card says Escalating. Mark urgent, in the card\'s ⋯ menu or behind a left swipe, moves it to Do First, or to Delegate if it isn\'t important. Nothing moves on its own. Change the window or turn it off in Settings › Appearance.</string>
    <string name="guide_keys">Keyboard shortcuts</string>
    <string name="guide_keys_palette">Open the command palette</string>
    <string name="guide_keys_search">Search in the command palette</string>
    <string name="guide_keys_new">New task</string>
    <string name="guide_keys_quadrant">Jump to a quadrant</string>
    <string name="guide_keys_close">Close a sheet</string>
    <string name="guide_gestures">Completing, editing, and moving</string>
    <string name="guide_complete_title">Complete</string>
    <string name="guide_complete_body">Tap the circle on a card, or swipe the card right. A recurring task then adds its next one.</string>
    <string name="guide_edit_title">Edit</string>
    <string name="guide_edit_body">Tap anywhere else on the card to open it in the editor.</string>
    <string name="guide_more_title">Everything else</string>
    <string name="guide_more_body">Tap a card\'s ⋯ button, or long-press it on a phone, to snooze, start a timer, duplicate, share, move, save, or delete it. Snooze runs from 15 minutes to Next week; Tomorrow and Next week mean a day and a week from now. Clear a snooze in the editor. Swipe a card left for Delete and Snooze, plus Mark urgent when it\'s escalating. A full swipe left snoozes it for an hour.</string>
    <string name="guide_drag_title">Move between quadrants</string>
    <string name="guide_drag_body">On a tablet\'s 2×2 board, long-press a card and drag it to another quadrant. On a phone, use Move to in the card\'s menu.</string>
    <string name="guide_keep">Saved, Trash, and Archive</string>
    <string name="guide_saved_title">Saved</string>
    <string name="guide_saved_body">Saved keeps a task out of the matrix until you\'re ready for it, like an article to read or an idea. Choose Move to Saved from a task\'s ⋯ menu, and find it under Saved in Browse. Add notes there, then choose Return to matrix to make it an active task again. Saved items don\'t show in the matrix or Smart Views and don\'t send reminders.</string>
    <string name="guide_trash_title">Undo and Trash</string>
    <string name="guide_trash_body">Deleting a task shows Undo for a few seconds. After that, the task waits in Trash, in Browse, for 30 days. Completed tasks move to Archive once they\'ve been done for 30, 60, or 90 days, the number you pick in Settings › Archive. Turn on auto-archive, or tap Archive now to do it once. Restore brings a task back from Trash or Archive.</string>
    <string name="guide_find">Finding things</string>
    <string name="guide_search_title">Search</string>
    <string name="guide_search_body">Tap Search in the Matrix top bar to search tasks, views, and actions, or to jump to Saved, Archive, or Settings. It matches task titles. The search at the top of Browse also looks in notes, tags, and subtasks.</string>
    <string name="guide_views_title">Smart Views</string>
    <string name="guide_views_body">Browse holds nine built-in Smart Views. Make your own with New Smart View, and pin up to five.</string>
    <string name="guide_select_title">Select several</string>
    <string name="guide_select_body">On the Matrix, tap the select button in the top bar, then tap tasks to complete, move, tag, date, or delete them together.</string>
    <string name="guide_sync">Cloud sync (optional)</string>
    <string name="guide_sync_body">Sync is off until you sign in. In Settings, sign in with Google, Apple, or GitHub, and your tasks sync across your devices and the web app through a self-hosted backend. Pull down on the Matrix to sync now.</string>
    <string name="guide_sync_chip">A chip in the Matrix bar appears only when there is something to know: a spinner while syncing, a count of changes waiting to go, or a warning when sync needs you. Sync history in Settings shows totals and your 50 most recent syncs.</string>
    <string name="guide_privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="guide_privacy_body">Your tasks live on this device, and GSD works fully offline with no account. Sync is opt-in, and fetching titles for links you share is a separate opt-in.</string>
    <string name="guide_site">Read more at gsdtaskmanager.com</string>
